menu "CDC Badge USB"

    config USB_EARLY_DEBUG
        bool "Start USB early for debugging"
        default n
        help
            When enabled, USB CDC starts immediately during boot for early debug output.
            This causes USB re-enumeration after modules are loaded, which may require
            unplugging and re-plugging the device on some hosts.

            When disabled (recommended for production), USB starts only after all
            modules are initialized, providing clean enumeration with all interfaces.

            Enable this only during development when you need boot-time debug logs.

endmenu
